Implement user story AMSD-2041: [GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Story Description
[GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Acceptance Criteria
- 


## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`Stack`): This is where the Contentstack SDK Stack is initialized. Live preview requires the SDK to be configured with live_preview options (enable:true, host) at Stack creation time. Without this, no downstream component can receive live preview events — the SDK itself won't subscribe to the preview delivery stream. Every content fetch flows through this Stack instance.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add live_preview configuration to the options object before it is passed to contentstack.Stack() on line 69. The options object (defined above the gap around lines 30-68) needs a live_preview key: live_preview: { enable: true, host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST } where CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST is read from process.env (add it alongside the existing CONTENTSTACK_API_HOST env var destructuring around line 23). This enables the Contentstack SDK's built-in live preview websocket subscription.
- **src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx** (`ContentstackProvider`): The provider currently memoizes defaultContent once and never updates it. For live preview, the context must react to Contentstack SDK live-preview events and push updated content to all consumers (236+ components via useContent). This is the runtime side of live preview: the SDK fires livePreviewUpdate callbacks, and the provider must listen and re-render with the new content.
  - **Minimal fix:** Replace the static useMemo with useState(defaultContent) for content, and add a useEffect that subscribes to the Contentstack SDK's live preview update events (Stack.live_preview.on('update', callback) or the @contentstack/live-preview-utils onEntryUpdate helper). On each event, merge the updated entry into the existing content state so all useContent consumers re-render with fresh data. The subscription should be cleaned up on unmount.


## Verification Criteria (what a tester will CONFIRM — your change must satisfy every one)
These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- A tester opens the preview site, edits an unpublished draft entry in the CMS, and observes the edited content appear on the rendered preview page without publishing the entry.
- A tester edits an entry in the CMS while a preview page is open and observes the change appear on that page without performing a full browser reload.
- A tester editing content in the CMS observes the update reflected on the GO Transit preview site.
- A tester editing content in the CMS observes the update reflected on the UP Express preview site.
- A tester editing content in the CMS observes the update reflected on the MX preview site.
- A tester makes several successive edits to the same entry in the CMS and observes each successive change appear on the preview page in turn.
- Text, images, and other entry fields rendered anywhere on a preview page reflect the latest CMS edit without a page reload.
- Content that was not edited in the CMS continues to render correctly on the preview page after other entries have been live-updated.
- A tester observes that an entry which has not been published still renders on the preview site with its latest in-progress edits, while the published content remains unchanged on the live site.

## Tests are NOT your job this turn
A dedicated test-writer agent runs immediately after your fix commits and owns the bug-reproducing test. Do NOT write, edit, or create any test file (*.test.*, *.spec.*, __tests__/). Write ONLY the fix. Adding a test here wastes your turn budget and has caused repeated failures.

